{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 27, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1\nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A WELL-KNOWN QUOTE OF THE FRENCH ACTIVIST AND PHILOSOPHER JEAN-PAUL SARTRE. HOWEVER, FROM A CRITIQUE STANDPOINT, THE SENTENCE CAN BE SEEN AS BEING TOO BLUNT AND OVERSIMPLISTIC. IT FAILS TO TAKE INTO ACCOUNT THE COMPLEXITIES OF REAL-WORLD SITUATIONS AND THE CONSEQUENCES OF DISOBEDIENCE. IN PRACTICE, DISOBEYING A LAW CAN LEAD TO UNINTENDED CONSEQUENCES, SUCH AS INJURY TO ONESELF OR OTHERS, OR EVEN LEADING TO THE LAW BECOMING EVEN MORE RESTRICTIVE.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2\nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE ALSO LACKS CLARITY AND SPECIFICITY. WHAT EXACTLY DOES \"BAD\" MEAN IN THIS CONTEXT? IS IT A SUBJECTIVE JUDGMENT OR AN OBJECTIVE ASSESSMENT? IS IT THE INTENT BEHIND THE LAW, OR THE EFFECT IT HAS ON INDIVIDUALS OR SOCIETY? WITHOUT A CLEAR DEFINITION OF WHAT \"BAD\" MEANS, THE SENTENCE IS LEFT OPEN TO INTERPRETATION, LEADING TO DISAGREEMENT AND CONFUSION. A MORE EFFECTIVE APPROACH WOULD BE TO PROVIDE A MORE THOUGHTFUL AND COMPREHENSIVE ANALYSIS OF THE COMPLEX RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN LAW AND MORALITY.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -0.0023090388}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -0.00035089056}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -0.000283082}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0047079194}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.5299425e-06}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.16702348}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.58440435}, {"token": " SENT", "logprob": -0.23184392}, {"token": "ENCE", "logprob": -3.0517112e-05}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.578928}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -0.0030436642}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": -8.344616e-06}, {"token": " LAW", "logprob": -0.00019369634}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": -3.4331686e-05}, {"token": " BAD", "logprob": -4.9470633e-05}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00059146073}, {"token": " YOU", "logprob": -0.00012623466}, {"token": " SHOULD", "logprob": -0.00040892346}, {"toke